            <div xml:id="d443">

                <pb facs="0627" n="503" xml:id="pg503"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/3268: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Crane</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-02-18T19:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 18,
                                1921—7 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received February 18—12:25
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>93. Quo Tai-chi on behalf of Canton Government requests that the Legation point
                    out to the Department that the accumulated Southern customs surpluses were
                    allocated with Peking Government’s consent withdrawal of which is retroactive
                    and <hi rendition="#italic">ultra vires</hi>, same argument applying to position
                    of the diplomatic body which has recently rejected Peking’s application for
                    these funds. I have no comment.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Crane</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
